<title>SINGAPORE: Republic Hotels 1996 net falls 5.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Republic Hotels 1996 net falls 5.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			  22.19    vs    23.43</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		 5.00    vs     5.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		  7.80    vs     8.20</p>
<p>    Turnover			   139.57    vs   128.70</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest    2.90    vs     1.95</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		 3.73    vs     1.92</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	  17.81    vs    15.60</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	  1.04    vs	-</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		    31.15    vs    33.48</p>
<p>    Tax				   10.14    vs    10.04</p>
<p>Dividend pay/register date: to be announced</p>
<p>Note - Republic Hotels &amp; Resorts Ltd attributed the drop in pre-tax profit to increased competition, higher funding costs and lower operating capacity due to major renovation work at its Singapore hotels.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
